    "id": "01e3e2d1",
    "metadata": {},
-   "source": "## 7. Full fine-tune (still on AN4 data)\n\nSame data and the same `finetune_parakeet.py`, just a real (multi-epoch) run instead of the 1-epoch smoke test above.\n\n`batch_size=8` (not the yaml's default 16) and `max_epochs=5` (not 50): the earlier attempt at `batch_size=16` peaked GPU RAM at ~14.5/15GB on a T4 and the run died (checkpointing only happens once per completed epoch, so a mid-epoch OOM restart also loses that epoch's progress - `resume_if_exists` had nothing to resume from). Raise `batch_size` back up incrementally if the GPU has headroom (check the Colab Resources panel's GPU RAM graph while it runs), and raise `max_epochs` once it survives cleanly at this size.\n\nWrites to a separate `exp_dir` (`checkpoints_full`, not `checkpoints`) so it starts fresh from the pretrained checkpoint instead of resuming the smoke test's 1-epoch run.\n\nAN4 is small and narrow-vocabulary, so a great WER here isn't proof the model generalizes — this run validates that a multi-epoch schedule (data loading, checkpointing, validation loop) completes cleanly. The real signal comes once you swap in the real dataset (see Next steps)."
+   "source": [
+    "## 7. Full fine-tune (still on AN4 data)\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Same data and the same `finetune_parakeet.py`, just a real (multi-epoch) run instead of the 1-epoch smoke test above.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "`batch_size=8` (not the yaml's default 16) and `max_epochs=5` (not 50): the earlier attempt at `batch_size=16` peaked GPU RAM at ~14.5/15GB on a T4 and the run died (checkpointing only happens once per completed epoch, so a mid-epoch OOM restart also loses that epoch's progress - `resume_if_exists` had nothing to resume from). Raise `batch_size` back up incrementally if the GPU has headroom (check the Colab Resources panel's GPU RAM graph while it runs), and raise `max_epochs` once it survives cleanly at this size.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "Writes to a separate `exp_dir` (`checkpoints_full`, not `checkpoints`) so it starts fresh from the pretrained checkpoint instead of resuming the smoke test's 1-epoch run.\n",
+    "\n",
+    "AN4 is small and narrow-vocabulary, so a great WER here isn't proof the model generalizes — this run validates that a multi-epoch schedule (data loading, checkpointing, validation loop) completes cleanly. The real signal comes once you swap in the real dataset (see Next steps)."
+   ]
   },
   {
    "cell_type": "code",
